      "note": "One experimental problem with three printed task groups (1. Adjustments and Measurements, 2. Calculations, 3. Data analysis) transcribed as sections s1–s3; the untitled task 0 (write apparatus and sample numbers) has no points and is kept at the end of the problem statement. Where one printed task box has two rows with separate points (1-b, 1-c, 1-d, 1-e, 2-d), both rows are one part and each row's printed points are kept inline in italics; the part's points are their sum. The paper prints the label 1-c twice (the second box, R_min^(1), 0.1 pt) and 1-e twice (the δ box, 0.2 pt); both are kept as printed; because a section cannot hold two parts with the same label, each repeated box is merged with the preceding box of the same label into one part, with the text printed between them (Hint/Step 3, resp. the definition of γ and δ with Eq. (6)) kept in place and each box's printed points kept inline. No total is printed; the printed points add up to 20.0 (5.3 + 6.2 + 8.5). Figure 3 is referenced in the statement text (\"A schematic diagram of the setup is shown in Figure 3:\"); it and Figures 1, 2, 4 are problem-level crops. Printed forms kept verbatim: 'the absorption spectra shows' (agreement error kept as printed per D-P28), 'equals to', '600 line/mm', 'there is no error is associated with it', 'in dark', 'Step1:', 'Plank’s constant' (a misspelt name, never changed), 'J.s'. The answer sheets (Tables 1d, 1e, 2c, 2d, 3a, 3d) are not in this file. Solutions: in 1b the last line prints θ0 = Δr/(2a) rad = 0.007 rad = 0.4° (without Δ on the left) although the table gives Δθ0 = 0.4°; kept as printed. In 2d the solution table reports λmax(I_glass) and λmax(I_film) while the task asks for the wavelengths of minimum R; kept. In 3d the solution says 'using Fig. 3' for the y–x graph; kept. The final page of both PDFs is a Win2PDF evaluation notice and is not transcribed. Fresh GPT-6.1 Sol full-source reading: all 34 pages personally inspected (8 main question + 10 main key + 6 apparatus + 10 alternate key, including all four publisher notices). The two full official key editions contain the same printed content and are transcribed once; PDF and preview PNG hashes differ by edition. Appended native apparatus pages i–v as a companion section, preserving all seven source figures and all 24 legend items. Source figures remain the nine original public crops, personally inspected; anchors now appear at native printed locations, with all IDs retained. Every original task, merged repeated 1-c/1-e label, answer and key text preserved. No independent model checker. Missing blank answer sheets remain explicit in the public caveat."
